a startup read must not stall the application

CORRECTION to the previous patch. Bounding the coordination wait at five seconds removed the
infinite hang, and I reported that the empty library list under launchd therefore had a second
cause. It does not. The five second value WAS the remaining cause: the stall lands during startup,
at the moment the library first loads, and the application has a deadline of its own there.

Measured on iA Writer under launchd, capture bytes for the library list, 15787 empty against about
27000 populated:

    CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS=200    27047   populated
    CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS=500    27047   populated
    CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS=1000   15787   EMPTY
    CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS=2000   15787   EMPTY

so the application deadline sits between 500ms and 1000ms. The default becomes 250ms, a factor of
two below the largest value that worked. A local XPC round trip is well under a millisecond, so a
daemon that answers at all is not cut off, and the whole cost of an absent daemon is now a quarter
of a second once.

CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS overrides it, which is how the numbers above were taken and how the next such
question should be answered.

Verified at the default with no override: launchd on gives 27047 and the four files are on screen,
launchd off gives 26966 and is unchanged.

--- a/src/NSFileCoordinator.m
+++ b/src/NSFileCoordinator.m
@@ -93,6 +93,31 @@
 /* Latched once the daemon has failed to answer, so only the first caller pays the whole timeout. */
 static BOOL daemonUnresponsive = NO;
 
+/*
+ * How long a startup read may stall, which is the whole cost of an absent daemon. Measured on iA
+ * Writer under launchd, capture bytes for its library list: 200ms and 500ms both populate it, 1000ms
+ * and 2000ms leave it EMPTY, so the application has a deadline of its own between those. 250 keeps
+ * a factor of two below the largest value that worked, and a local XPC round trip is well under a
+ * millisecond, so nothing that answers at all is cut off. CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS overrides it.
+ */
+static int64_t _NSFileCoordinationTimeoutMsec(void)
+{
+	static int64_t msec = 250;
+	static dispatch_once_t once;
+
+	dispatch_once(&once, ^{
+		const char* value = getenv("CIDER_FC_TIMEOUT_MS");
+
+		if (value != NULL && value[0] != '\0') {
+			long parsed = strtol(value, NULL, 10);
+
+			if (parsed > 0) msec = parsed;
+		}
+	});
+
+	return msec;
+}
+
 static void handle_xpc_error(xpc_object_t error) {
 	// do nothing with it for now
 };
@@ -451,7 +476,7 @@
 		 * The first caller pays the full wait; once the daemon is known not to answer, later
 		 * callers pay a token wait instead of the whole timeout each.
 		 */
-		int64_t timeout = daemonUnresponsive ? (NSEC_PER_SEC / 10) : (5 * NSEC_PER_SEC);
+		int64_t timeout = daemonUnresponsive ? (NSEC_PER_SEC / 10) : (_NSFileCoordinationTimeoutMsec() * NSEC_PER_MSEC);
 
 		if (dispatch_semaphore_wait(waiter, dispatch_time(DISPATCH_TIME_NOW, timeout)) != 0) {
